3. GNU FreeFont / FreeSans (present legacy asset; successor bundling blocked)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The file data/fonts/README identifies GNU FreeFont and states that the fonts
are free software under the GNU GPL, version 3 or any later version, with a
special exception for documents embedding an unaltered font or unaltered
portions of it. It also states that FontForge .sfd files are the preferred
source for modification.

The repository contains data/fonts/FreeSans.ttf and that README but no .sfd
preferred source or documented source offer. This is an UNRESOLVED preferred-
source gap. It blocks bundling FreeSans.ttf in a new Rust/native release, not
development: development may use a system FreeSans or a separately supplied
font. Do not download the font at runtime. If FreeSans is later bundled, ship
its exact preferred source (or compliant source offer), README/license text,
and this notice together.

