5. External tools: FFmpeg and Git
----------------------------------

FFmpeg is planned as an external process for video encoding. Git is planned as
an external process/input source after custom-log ingestion. Neither binary is
bundled by this repository at this stage, and neither may be downloaded at
runtime. The user's FFmpeg build may be LGPL- or GPL-configured; a future
bundle would require auditing that exact build, its notices, and its
corresponding source. Git's own license applies to a Git binary if one is ever
bundled; invoking an external Git does not make it a project dependency.

Missing FFmpeg or Git must produce an actionable error or an explicitly
unsupported/deferred feature. Release archives must document the external
requirement without implying that the project distributes either binary.

